  "chosen": {
    "implementation": "createFixtureTemplate(connectionString) once right after migration, then resetFixture(connectionString) before every round",
    "method": "b_template",
    "reasons": [
      "Every round of a and b, including the first after the original suite, returned response bytes identical to the freshly migrated database and four passes, so neither shows state carried over in Umami memory for these requests.",
      "c restarts Umami and needs about 21 seconds per round, so 20 rounds take about 420 seconds, beyond the 240-second phase.",
      "b restores the whole database at the Postgres level, sequences and every table included, from a copy taken right after migration; a depends on a snapshot schema inside the application database and on the table list it read.",
      "b costs at most about 0.15 seconds per reset, about 0.1 seconds more than a; 20 rounds of b plus the slowest measured suite run stay within the phase."
    ],
    "requires": "a database role that may create and drop databases (the stack's own superuser role); the connection string is a parameter, never read from the environment"
  },
